          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपद्रवः — upadravaḥ — \"a disturbance; a riot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नगरे सहसा उपद्रवः घटितः। nagare sahasā upadravaḥ ghaṭitaḥ. A disturbance suddenly broke out in the city."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "उपद्रवः (upadravaḥ) is built from upa and the root √dru, \"to run\"; MW gives upadrava as that which attacks suddenly, a misfortune, and also national commotion or rebellion (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
